# Everything is LF in the repository and LF on checkout.
#
# This is not a style preference. templates/gate-runner.sh is a shipped bash
# script, and a CRLF checkout makes bash fail on it with a syntax error naming
# a token that ends in a carriage return - the same confusing failure this
# repository's own checker produced against itself for one commit, by writing
# to a text-mode pipe on Windows. A method repository that distributes a
# broken script is not in a position to give advice.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the executables, so an override elsewhere cannot reach
# them.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
